  ('r-s09', 'reading', 'vocabulary-in-context', 4, 'session', 'description', 'The committee''s report was notable less for its findings than for its candor: it openly listed the mistakes the agency had made and the warnings it had ignored.', 75, 'As used in the text, what does the word ''candor'' most nearly mean?', '["frankness", "length", "caution", "popularity"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The sentence explains ''candor'' right after the colon: the report openly listed mistakes and ignored warnings. That is frankness.', false),
  ('r-s10', 'reading', 'inferences', 5, 'session', 'discernment', 'Early telescopes could not resolve the faint, distant galaxy clusters that astronomers now catalog routinely. Some nineteenth-century astronomers therefore concluded that such clusters did not exist. Modern observations suggest that ______', 75, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the astronomers'' conclusion reflected the limits of their instruments rather than the absence of the clusters.", "nineteenth-century telescopes were more powerful than modern ones.", "galaxy clusters formed only after the nineteenth century.", "astronomers no longer catalog galaxy clusters."]'::jsonb, 0, 'Not seeing something with a weak tool is different from it not existing. Modern telescopes see the clusters, so the earlier conclusion came from the tool''s limits.', false)
